---
// Version anglaise de /confidentialite/ (politique de confidentialité, Loi 25). Traduction fidèle.
// La version française prévaut en cas de divergence (mention en haut de page).
// Note : baseline conforme Loi 25, pas un avis juridique. À faire réviser si besoin.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const siteUrl = Astro.site?.href.replace(/\/$/, '') ?? 'https://fournia.net';
const canonical = `${siteUrl}/en/privacy/`;
const maj = 'November 4, 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy policy | FournIA"
  description="How FournIA collects, uses and protects your personal information, in compliance with Quebec's privacy law (Law 25)."
  canonical={canonical}
  lang="en"
>
  <main>
    <article class="post">
      <div class="wrap-narrow">
        <nav class="crumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> <span>/</span> Privacy</nav>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="meta">Last updated: {maj}</p>
        <p class="traduction">This is a translation. In case of discrepancy, the <a href="/confidentialite/" hreflang="fr-CA" lang="fr">French version</a> prevails.</p>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            FournIA (Simon Fournier, a business registered in Quebec, NEQ 2282026550) cares about
            protecting your personal information. This policy explains what information we collect,
            why, who it is shared with and what rights you have, in accordance with Quebec's privacy
            law (Law 25) (An Act to modernize legislative provisions as regards the protection of
            personal information).
          </p>

          <h2>Person in charge of the protection of personal information</h2>
          <p>
            Simon Fournier is the person in charge of the protection of personal information at
            FournIA. For any question or request: <a href="mailto:s.fournier@fournia.net">s.fournier@fournia.net</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>Information we collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>When you book a call</strong> (through the SaaS AI System calendar): your name, your email address, and any information you give us about your business and your needs.</li>
            <li><strong>When you fill out a form</strong> (on the site or in a Meta ad): the contact details and answers you enter.</li>
            <li><strong>When you browse the site</strong>: technical data (pages viewed, device, source of the visit) through cookies and measurement tools, including the Meta pixel and Google Analytics.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We only collect what is needed to answer you and prepare a possible engagement. We do not ask for sensitive information.</p>

          <h2>Why we use it</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>To communicate with you, schedule and hold the discovery call or the assessment.</li>
            <li>To understand your needs and prepare a recommendation or a proposal.</li>
            <li>To measure the performance of our ads and improve the site.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not use your information for any other purpose without your consent.</p>

          <h2>Cookies, Meta pixel, Google Analytics and visit tracking</h2>
          <p>
            The site uses cookies and the Meta pixel (Facebook, Instagram) to measure the
            effectiveness of our ads and show relevant content. <strong>These tools stay turned off
            until you accept them</strong> in the consent banner shown on your first visit. You can
            change your mind at any time with the "Manage cookies" link at the bottom of every page,
            delete cookies in your browser, and manage your ad preferences directly in your Meta
            account. Refusing cookies does not prevent you from booking a call.
          </p>
          <p>
            The site also uses a tracking script from our customer relationship management platform,
            SaaS AI System. It measures pages viewed and forms filled out. If you send us your contact
            details through a form, your visits may be linked to your file so that we can better
            answer your request. This tracking only turns on if you accept cookies. The chat bubble,
            however, is always available: the messages you write there reach us in the same platform.
          </p>
          <p>
            We also use Google Analytics to measure traffic to the site: pages viewed, where visits
            come from, type of device, clicks on the booking button and forms sent. We do not send it
            your name or your email. Like the other measurement tools, Google Analytics only turns on
            if you accept cookies.
          </p>
          <p>
            The first replies in the chat bubble are written by an artificial intelligence assistant,
            based on the public content of this site. It can answer your general questions and book a
            discovery call. It makes no decision about you: Simon Fournier reads the conversations and
            takes over as soon as you ask. Your messages are processed by the SaaS AI System platform,
            in the United States.
          </p>

          <h2>Sharing and transfers outside Quebec</h2>
          <p>
            We never sell your information. We use providers based outside Quebec to run our tools.
            By submitting your information, you understand that it may be processed outside Quebec,
            under the agreements of these providers:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Meta</strong> (ads, pixel): United States.</li>
            <li><strong>Google</strong> (Google Analytics, traffic measurement): United States.</li>
            <li><strong>Calendly</strong> (old appointment booking links, being phased out): United States.</li>
            <li><strong>HubSpot</strong> (customer relationship management): United States.</li>
            <li><strong>SaaS AI System</strong> (customer relationship management, appointment booking, site visit tracking, chat): United States.</li>
            <li><strong>Google</strong> (email, calendar): United States.</li>
            <li><strong>Netlify</strong> (site hosting): United States.</li>
            <li><strong>Twilio</strong> (sending text messages / SMS): United States.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We limit the information sent to these tools to what is strictly necessary.</p>

          <h2>Text messaging (SMS)</h2>
          <p>
            If you consent to receive text messages from FournIA or from a FournIA client (for
            example follow-up reminders from your advisor), the following terms apply:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>We do not sell or share your mobile phone numbers or your SMS opt-in data with third
              parties for marketing or promotional purposes.</li>
            <li>Message frequency varies: usually a few messages per year (follow-up reminders and one follow-up message), depending on your file.</li>
            <li>Message and data rates may apply.</li>
            <li>You can unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP, and get help by replying AIDE
              (French for "help").</li>
            <li>Messages are delivered through our provider Twilio (United States).</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Retention</h2>
          <p>
            We keep your information for as long as needed to follow up on your request and, where
            applicable, for the length of our business relationship. When it is no longer required,
            we delete or anonymize it.
          </p>

          <h2>Security</h2>
          <p>
            We take reasonable measures to protect your information against loss and unauthorized
            access. Your information is never stored in plain text in a public code repository.
          </p>

          <h2>Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You can at any time request access to your information, its correction or its deletion,
            and withdraw your consent. Write to us at
            <a href="mailto:s.fournier@fournia.net">s.fournier@fournia.net</a> and we will follow up
            within the time limits set by law. If you are not satisfied, you can file a complaint
            with the Commission d'accès à l'information du Québec (CAI).
          </p>

          <h2>Changes</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy. The date of the last update appears at the top of the page.
          </p>

          <h2>Contact us</h2>
          <p>
            FournIA, Simon Fournier<br />
            <a href="mailto:s.fournier@fournia.net">s.fournier@fournia.net</a><br />
            <a href="tel:+15148632973">514 863 2973</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  main { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .post { padding: 8.5rem 0 4rem; }
  .wrap-narrow { width: min(760px, 92vw); margin: 0 auto; }
  .crumbs { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--mute-d); margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--lime); }
  .crumbs span { margin: 0 .4rem; }
  .post h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.1rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -.02em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--mute-d); font-size: .92rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .prose { color: var(--mute); font-size: 1.06rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .prose :global(h2) { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; color: var(--white); font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 2.4rem 0 .9rem; }
  .prose :global(p) { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .prose :global(ul) { margin: 0 0 1.2rem 1.3rem; }
  .prose :global(li) { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .prose :global(a) { color: var(--lime); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; text-decoration-color: rgba(183,217,76,.4); }
  .prose :global(a:hover) { text-decoration-color: var(--lime); }
  .prose :global(strong) { color: var(--white); font-weight: 600; }
  .traduction { color: var(--mute-d); font-size: .9rem; font-style: italic; margin: -1.2rem 0 2rem; }
  .traduction a { color: var(--lime); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
</style>
